        "The engagement itself was brief, almost anticlimactic given the six years of history behind it. My men engaged the lead vehicles exactly as planned, drawing attention and fire toward the front of the convoy, creating precisely the kind of chaos that makes a man in the third vehicle feel, briefly, safe enough to step out and observe his own ambush unfolding.",
        "Marco Castellano made that mistake. He climbed out of the third vehicle to get a better view of what he believed was his moment of triumph, standing exposed at the treeline's edge for perhaps four full seconds before he understood, too late, that the entire skirmish in front of him had been a diversion built around exactly this moment of exposure.",
        "I took the shot from ninety meters, a single round, the kind of precision that comes only from a decade of deliberate practice rather than luck or improvisation. He was dead before his men fully understood what had happened, before the echo of the shot had finished rolling across the treeline. Six years of feud, generations of accumulated grievance between two families, ended in the time it takes to exhale once, slowly, and pull a trigger.",
        "We were gone before his remaining men regrouped enough to give proper chase, back across the border into territory that has never once, in seven years, failed to protect me. Dimitri didn't speak until we were well clear, and when he finally did, it was with the particular satisfaction of two men who've spent a decade being underestimated by people who mistook patience for weakness.",
        "\"Six years,\" he said. \"Ended in four seconds.\"",
