        "I took her the way I take most things offered to me freely — thoroughly, without cruelty but without gentleness either, my hands finding her hips and pinning her against the cold stone of the bedroom wall, her breath catching sharp against my ear, the whole encounter conducted with the same total, competent precision I bring to everything else in my life, including the two deaths that had preceded it by mere hours.",
        "She enjoyed it. I understand, distantly, that most women do. What I felt, watching her dress afterward with the flushed, satisfied looseness of someone who believes she's just touched something significant, was the same hollowness I always feel in these moments — a hollowness that neither Sergei's death nor Marco's had touched, that her body against mine didn't touch either, that nothing in seven years has managed to touch at all.",
